  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Utah has $50.1M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government made 211 awards in Utah so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $238K. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows large swings before FY2027: FY22 registered $5.3B, FY23 registered $6.3B, FY24 registered $7.2B, FY25 registered $5.2B, and FY26 registered $7B. The current-year total is partial and covers fiscal year to date. Spending in FY2027 to date is concentrated: the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $37.2M and the Department of Housing and Urban Development obligated $10.9M. Vendor concentration is clear: BIOMERIEUX INC received $20.7M and ALPINE COMPANIES, INC. received $10.9M. Industry concentration mirrors vendor totals: In-Vitro Diagnostic Substance Manufacturing received $19.7M and Residential Property Managers received $10.9M. This snapshot shows a much smaller FY2027 to date total compared with prior full fiscal years and a high concentration of obligations in a few agencies, vendors, and industries.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 spending compare to prior years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $50.1M. FY22 obligations were $5.3B, FY23 obligations were $6.3B, FY24 obligations were $7.2B, FY25 obligations were $5.2B, and FY26 obligations were $7B. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. The current FY2027 total is partial and covers fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors drive FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $37.2M and the Department of Housing and Urban Development obligated $10.9M. The Department of Agriculture obligated $1.2M and the Department of Justice obligated $799K. BIOMERIEUX INC received $20.7M and ALPINE COMPANIES, INC. received $10.9M. The UNIVERSITY OF UTAH received $7.6M and GOVTRANZ, LLC received $4.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
